1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sun setting
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,920
Would you care to listen for a moment?

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,140
They laughed at me for
still acting like a kid.

5
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I try to stir
up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
a yawn here and there changes nothing.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,440
the sun sinks into the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:15,920
Why does tomorrow have to end too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:20,980
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness is lost again.

12
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,320
The demon of traffic safety.

13
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:38,380
I'm running out of steam here.

14
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:40,220
Just let it slide this once, won't you?

15
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:40,660
Please.

16
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:42,420
No way.

17
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:45,360
It's people like you that
keep accidents from going down.

18
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:49,480
I just bought it, so I hadn't gotten
a feel for the accelerator yet.

19
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:52,964
Whether it's a used car or a dump truck,

20
00:01:53,014 --> 00:01:55,840
or an F1 car, speeding is speeding!

21
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,360
So bicycles are fine, then?

22
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,740
Dage dage dage dage dage dage!

23
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,720
Good work on the crackdown!

24
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,120
Alright, Kankichi!

25
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:14,840
Yeah, that's right.
I'm just on my way to the traffic section.

26
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,760
What business do you have with our section?

27
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:20,220
Shinshin, when you come in,
the air in this room gets dirty.

28
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:22,040
I don't want to go.

29
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,420
By Chief Ohara's orders,

30
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,960
I've been made to receive
traffic safety guidance.

31
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:29,840
Traffic safety guidance?

32
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,960
So, from the traffic section,

33
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,620
how was it read again?

34
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:37,240
Ishizu Tetsuo...

35
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,780
Chief Ishizu Tetsuo.

36
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:40,540
That's right.

37
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:42,400
It's Ishizu, Ishizu.

38
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,880
I have to receive individual
guidance from that man.

39
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,520
What on earth is this supposed to be?

40
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:51,440
What's the matter?

41
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:54,180
I was just trying to ask about Chief Ishizu,

42
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:55,060
I see.

43
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:58,820
You went to Chief Ishizu's place,

44
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:01,500
you repulsive cockroach of a guy, but

45
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:02,760
how pitiful.

46
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,200
What's with that reaction?

47
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,060
Same here.

48
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:10,420
we may never see each other again,

49
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:11,300
goodbye.

50
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,240
Hey, wait!

51
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:21,140
I don't understand a thing.

52
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,420
Chief Ishizu?

53
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,880
Honestly, what kind of old guy is he?

54
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,624
No way,

55
00:03:31,674 --> 00:03:36,060
Ryo-sama being sent to
Chief Ishizu's place, no way,

56
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:38,660
Why are you reacting like that?

57
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:40,980
Ryo-sama,

58
00:03:41,030 --> 00:03:45,860
Maria will never forget you, Ryo-sama.

59
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:46,560
Hey, wait!

60
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:51,360
What is going on?

61
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,280
I came to see Chief Ishizu.

62
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:06,320
What business do you have with Chief Ishizu?

63
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,960
I came to receive traffic safety guidance.

64
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:11,340
Traffic safety guidance.

65
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,180
Where am I? Who am I?

66
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:18,000
Not again.

67
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:21,020
Hey! What kind of guy is Chief Ishizu?

68
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,480
Tell me! What kind of guy is he?

69
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,820
Is he really that terrifying?

70
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:30,100
Excuse me, could you let me through there?

71
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,000
We're busy right now!

72
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,800
Chief Ishizu...

73
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,440
What!?

74
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:38,760
Excuse me!

75
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:41,060
Sorry about that.

76
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,040
He looks like a nice old guy.

77
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,960
Oof, alright then, let's see.

78
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:54,440
Chief Ishizu, Senior Officer Ryotsu from the
Kameari Park police box is here to see you.

79
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:59,520
I see. This horse is tough to read,
you know.

80
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:02,120
Chief Ishizu, you bet on the horses too?

81
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:07,160
Yes, horse racing is great.
I just love horses.

82
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,660
Well, I'm glad you're a man who understands.

83
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:14,200
To celebrate getting to know each other,
let's head to the racetrack together today.

84
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:18,120
Just say we did the traffic safety guidance,
more or less.

85
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:20,140
Traffic safety guidance?

86
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:22,940
I'll go get ready for a sec.

87
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:25,580
Are you changing your clothes?

88
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,120
Retail use only?

89
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:35,500
Hey, hey.

90
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:40,380
What on earth is going on?

91
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,700
What's this?

92
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:46,000
It was truly the end of the century.

93
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,240
Humanity was facing the brink of extinction.

94
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:52,380
Due to a battle called the traffic war,

95
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:53,364
But,

96
00:05:53,414 --> 00:05:58,240
a single savior appeared here.

97
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,280
W-what?

98
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,620
W-what are you?

99
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:18,960
Known as the walking
traffic law for 35 years,

100
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:22,640
seventh-dan master of
traffic safety guidance.

101
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:25,800
Ishizu Tetsuo Kenzō.

102
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,240
So you're Chief Ishizu?

103
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,320
Indeed.

104
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:33,340
You're a completely different person!

105
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,561
You there,

106
00:06:34,611 --> 00:06:39,220
you just made light of traffic safety guidance,
didn't you?

107
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:42,120
That? I just slipped up and said it.

108
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:45,780
Even though you're a police
officer who guides the citizens,

109
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:46,840
I can't forgive that!

110
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:51,800
Dance of the Traffic Tickets,
Arc-Kip Chapter!

111
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:52,360
Whoa!

112
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,600
This is unbearable!

113
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:54,300
Not letting you escape!

114
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:57,960
Art of Halting the Violator!

115
00:06:58,720 --> 00:06:59,340
Whoa!

116
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:00,300
Let go!

117
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:02,120
Gah, gah, whoa!

118
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Don't suddenly let go, you idiot!

119
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:05,600
Gyaaaah!

120
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,940
You're going to get a full dose of

121
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:10,720
the traffic safety spirit drilled into you!

122
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:21,520
Why do I have to dress up like this too?

123
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:26,400
That's the uniform for Seventh Class
of Ishizuru-ryu Traffic Safety Guidance.

124
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,820
Ishizuru-ryu Traffic Safety Guidance?

125
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:30,640
What's that supposed to be?

126
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:37,040
I established it to spread proper
traffic safety throughout the nation.

127
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:40,000
By the way, armor is only
permitted from first dan onward.

128
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,440
Only those who have been granted an exemption for
store-bought signals and sirens are permitted to use them.

129
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:48,440
It's so loud I can't hear a thing!

130
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:51,100
As a beginner, you start at seventh class.

131
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:56,260
Each time you properly master the traffic laws,
you'll be promoted through sixth class, fifth class, and so on.

132
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:59,260
Nobody wants to be promoted!

133
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:01,940
Ishizuru-ryu Traffic Safety Guidance

134
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:04,760
First, how to cross a pedestrian crosswalk.

135
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,840
Go on, try it.

136
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:12,020
If no cars are coming,
you just cross the crosswalk quickly, right?

137
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:12,620
Wrong.

138
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,120
What is this?

139
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,420
What are you doing?

140
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:22,620
You should have learned
this in elementary school.

141
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:30,620
When crossing at a crosswalk, look right, look left,
look right again, then raise your hand and cross.

142
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:32,180
Try it again.

143
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:33,960
Fine, I get it.

144
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:38,560
Look right, look left,
then look right again,

145
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:41,180
raise your hand, and cross.

146
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,920
This is right, isn't it?

147
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,380
Not good enough.

148
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:50,600
Finally,
I did it exactly as you told me, didn't I?

149
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:54,980
Do you really think
safety is ensured by that?

150
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:58,280
And when there's a flag,
you must properly raise a flag.

151
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:00,260
Where's the flag?

152
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,120
So it was a flag.

153
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:10,500
You lack the mindset to truly

154
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:13,780
check whether it's really safe.

155
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,780
I'll show you an example.

156
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:16,800
Watch closely.

157
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:21,760
Ishizuru-ryu:
The Proper Way to Cross at a Crosswalk

158
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:23,640
Checking the signal.

159
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:25,620
All green, path clear!

160
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:28,420
Checking right.

161
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:30,280
No vehicles approaching.

162
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:34,460
Check left.

163
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:36,700
No moving vehicles.

164
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:37,840
Then right.

165
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,580
No moving vehicles.

166
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:42,640
Safety confirmed.

167
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:42,980
Good.

168
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,140
Left hand.

169
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:46,700
Shoulder good.

170
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,620
Right hand up.

171
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:50,020
Start walking.

172
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:54,200
The right arm angle is 75 degrees upward.

173
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:57,140
It's an angle that drivers
behind you can clearly see.

174
00:09:57,140 --> 00:10:00,200
Because the steel is coated
with fluorescent paint.

175
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:07,840
Known as the walking
traffic law for 35 years,

176
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,360
this is Ishizuru-ryu.

177
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:12,920
This is the proper way
to cross at a crosswalk.

178
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:18,220
To think it takes this much
just to cross a crosswalk!

179
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:22,780
You really lack seriousness, you know.

180
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:26,120
It seems we'd better go out into town
and give you guidance in practice.

181
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,620
This is my beloved car.

182
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:29,420
W-what is this?

183
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:29,600
This is...!

184
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:34,520
A large rearview mirror that lets you
better check for safety in the distance.

185
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:38,520
An oversized turn signal designed
so others won't overlook it.

186
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:41,120
Training wheels to prevent tipping over.

187
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:45,660
There are all sorts of other
safety features built in as well.

188
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:52,340
This is the definitive 1998
safety-enhanced vehicle!

189
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:55,260
It's the Ishizuru-ryu Hyper White Bike!

190
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:59,560
For a bike with such a grand name,
it's pretty ugly, isn't it?

191
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,560
Idiot!

192
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,760
With vehicles,
safety comes before appearance!

193
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:07,140
Looking back at the
history of the 20th century,

194
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:12,200
there were far too many accidents
caused by neglecting safety.

195
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,620
You could even call it the
century of traffic accidents.

196
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,420
Yeah, that's true.

197
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:20,920
The coming 21st century must
become a century of traffic safety!

198
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:27,540
As a first step, I spent my own
money modifying this motorcycle.

199
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:33,960
Naturally, I tried to modify other motorcycles too,
but for some reason everyone refuses.

200
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:39,340
For a police officer, your awareness
of traffic safety is far too low.

201
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:42,980
This thing's so heavy,
won't it be dangerous to ride back?

202
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,820
Do you have a motorcycle license?

203
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:47,360
I have one, technically.

204
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:51,400
Since we're here, I'll teach you how
to ride an Ishizuru-ryu motorcycle.

205
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:52,900
Get on and try it.

206
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:53,880
Yeah, yeah.

207
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:55,080
Here goes.

208
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:56,620
How's that?

209
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:57,320
You idiot!

210
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:57,700
No way.

211
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,840
Once you're on the motorcycle,
put on your seatbelt right away!

212
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:04,080
I've never heard of a
seatbelt on a motorcycle.

213
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,760
My motorcycle has one.

214
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:07,180
What?

215
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:08,260
So it does.

216
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:10,820
This is it, right?

217
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:13,280
That's not the only seatbelt.

218
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,280
So there's a double seatbelt?

219
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:21,480
As expected of the seventh-generation motorcycle
of the master traffic safety instructor.

220
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:24,020
There's still more than that.

221
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:25,800
There's more?

222
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,420
There's another one here too!

223
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,380
And here too,

224
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:29,360
and here,

225
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:31,120
and here as well!

226
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,340
And here,

227
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:32,860
and here,

228
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:33,340
and here,

229
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:34,280
and here too!

230
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:36,480
This is the ultimate in safety!

231
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,900
It's a 36-point seatbelt!

232
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:42,040
With this, up, down,
left, right, front, and back

233
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,260
can withstand any impact.

234
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:47,360
But with this,
you can't move at all, you know!

235
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:01,520
Now, next, grip the handlebars.

236
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:03,920
Pretend you're actually driving.

237
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:05,780
How does it feel?

238
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:06,780
Shoo -

239
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,760
How is it different?

240
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:10,480
Listen closely.

241
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:13,020
First, your back must be at 90 degrees.

242
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,940
Fingers at 78 degrees, arms at 65 degrees,

243
00:13:16,990 --> 00:13:20,220
legs at 115 degrees, knees at 62 degrees.

244
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:23,780
This is the correct way to ride a motorcycle,
according to Ishizuru-ryu!

245
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:27,640
Honestly, he treats people's
bodies like they're nothing!

246
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:33,440
What's this?
This speedometer only goes up to 60 km!

247
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:34,926
Of course,

248
00:13:34,976 --> 00:13:38,380
the speed limit on Japanese roads is 60 kilometers per hour,
after all.

249
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:40,300
Anything more is unnecessary.

250
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,720
That's only for ordinary roads, right?

251
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,780
What about expressways?

252
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,160
On expressways...

253
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:49,400
"Don't speed, obey the limit,
protect your own life."

254
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:51,700
Even after coming up with
traffic slogans like that,

255
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:54,480
they go out of their way to
build roads where you can speed.

256
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:58,240
What on earth is the government thinking?

257
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:01,560
It's because of things like that that
accidents aren't decreasing at all!

258
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:04,560
I'm never using expressways
for the rest of my life!

259
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,680
You're awfully set in your ways, aren't you.

260
00:14:11,860 --> 00:14:13,620
Now then,
let's actually go out into the street.

261
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,920
Which one is my motorcycle?

262
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:17,120
You idiot!

263
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:19,720
In Ishizuru-ryu traffic safety guidance,

264
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:22,320
only those of third dan and
above may ride a motorcycle.

265
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,080
Then what am I supposed to do?

266
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:26,980
Seventh-rank people have to run.

267
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:27,680
What?

268
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:31,940
Hey, Chief Ishizu, what's going on?

269
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,660
Hurry up and follow me.

270
00:14:33,660 --> 00:14:35,640
Let go of me, it's dangerous!

271
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,520
Don't joke around, seriously!

272
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:45,940
Not good!

273
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:48,980
Ugh, so annoying!

274
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:54,100
What, you waited for me?

275
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:59,240
Right in front of Ishizuru Tetsuo,
seventh-dan traffic safety instructor!

276
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:01,260
Unforgivable!

277
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:04,460
The dance of the penalty tickets.

278
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:06,100
Red tickets for him!

279
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:08,400
What did I even do?

280
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:09,960
He ran a red light!

281
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:13,740
When I crossed, it was green.

282
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:16,300
It was flashing green, wasn't it?

283
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:18,320
I saw you properly in the rearview mirror.

284
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:20,840
You finished crossing before it turned fully red,
didn't you?

285
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:21,260
You!

286
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:24,120
Don't you even know what a
flashing green light means?

287
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:27,880
Doesn't it mean it's about to turn red?

288
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:28,560
Wrong.

289
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:30,400
Follow me.

290
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:34,760
First, when you've already
entered the crosswalk,

291
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:38,700
if the signal starts flashing,
you hurry across.

292
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:47,300
Isn't that armor too heavy?

293
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,300
This protects my body.

294
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:52,140
I can't let it go.

295
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:53,760
Do whatever you want.

296
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:58,440
If it's before you enter the crosswalk,

297
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,360
stop.

298
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:02,960
Come here.

299
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:03,760
You're in the way.

300
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,680
Chief Ishizu!

301
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:11,840
Damn you!

302
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:14,380
Because of people like you,

303
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:17,340
Japan's traffic order is falling apart.

304
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:18,700
Please, stop it.

305
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:19,760
It's red, red!

306
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:23,660
Are you all right?

307
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:27,240
Thanks to the armor,
I don't have a scratch on me!

308
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:32,280
But if you hadn't had that armor on in the first place,
you wouldn't have fallen over, would you?

309
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:36,060
Next is how to cross a railroad crossing.

310
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:37,340
Go on, try it.

311
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:40,380
The basics are the same
as a crosswalk, right?

312
00:16:40,780 --> 00:16:42,260
Please lend me the binoculars.

313
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:43,460
No way.

314
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:46,240
You're only allowed to use
binoculars from first rank onward.

315
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,900
Until then,
check carefully with your own eyes.

316
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:50,360
You really are picky about all these details,
aren't you.

317
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,160
Right, clear.

318
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:55,820
Left, clear.

319
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:57,700
Right again, clear.

320
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:01,660
Matto!

321
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,920
You did check properly, didn't you?

322
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:10,520
At a railroad crossing,
there's an additional procedure.

323
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:13,860
Trains move much faster than cars.

324
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:15,980
They come up in no time at all.

325
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:20,800
So you press your ear
to the rails and check.

326
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:23,920
This is the Ishizuru-style way
to cross a railroad crossing!

327
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:26,900
Is it really necessary to go that far?

328
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,880
Hey! Get out of the way already!

329
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:36,400
We're in the middle of traffic safety instruction!
Wait quietly!

330
00:17:36,460 --> 00:17:37,720
We're in a hurry here!

331
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:38,820
What did you say?

332
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:43,160
Drivers like you are the ones
who wreck the traffic order!

333
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:47,180
If you're in a hurry, take an airplane!

334
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,340
Impatient people aren't
suited to be drivers!

335
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:52,080
Impatience is a loss!
Always keep your heart at ease!

336
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:53,200
Got it?

337
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:57,960
Modern people are so short-tempered

338
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:01,920
Spread Ishizuru-ryu traffic safety
instruction nationwide as soon as possible!

339
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,080
Are you all right?

340
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:09,020
Thanks to the armor, I was saved.

341
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,740
It's because of that armor you didn't notice the warning,
isn't it?

342
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,460
Hey!

343
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:18,960
Not watching ahead is a violation of the duty of safe driving,
you know!

344
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:21,800
It's certainly sturdy, I'll give you that.

345
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:24,380
What?

346
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:31,400
What a guy who keeps getting run over.

347
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:37,600
Hit-and-run, speeding, violating lane designations,
failing to stop at a railroad crossing.

348
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:42,140
On top of that, we absolutely
cannot let a hit-and-run slide.

349
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,880
I'll punish him!

350
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,600
Don't leave me behind!

351
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:51,140
Come on, seventh-rank officer,
run and chase after them!

352
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:52,860
This is an emergency, you know!

353
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:54,680
Can't be helped.

354
00:18:58,020 --> 00:18:59,500
Why are you stopping?

355
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:02,580
Look, the light's red!

356
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:04,820
We're in pursuit of a suspect!

357
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:06,980
This is no time for that!

358
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:09,540
No matter what,
I always obey the traffic laws.

359
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:11,340
This is Ishizuru-style.

360
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:17,160
You told me to wait, and now we've lost him!

361
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,520
Don't worry, I've got him on data.

362
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:22,400
Data.

363
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:29,460
I'm detecting the faint radio waves from the self-restoring
paint on that armor that stuck to me when he hit me.

364
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:32,040
You're a tricky one, aren't you?

365
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:35,520
But if you're using all that
high-tech completely wrong...

366
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,600
He's pulling away!

367
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:39,760
Please speed up.

368
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,260
This road has a 30 km/h limit.

369
00:19:42,260 --> 00:19:44,000
We've got the siren on, you know!

370
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,020
Surely it's fine in a situation like this!

371
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:48,900
No matter what anyone says,
the speed limit gets lowered.

372
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:50,740
That's Ishizuru-ryu!

373
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:54,380
What are you doing?

374
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:55,640
Lead up!

375
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:56,440
Right!

376
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,800
Idiot! Stop! Cut it out!

377
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:01,620
I won't stop!

378
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,900
Stop! Stop it!

379
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,660
What's going on?

380
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:20,937
What kind of girl evades the
pursuit of Lord Ishizu like this?

381
00:20:20,987 --> 00:20:22,060
A blade of a hundred years!

382
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:43,520
Let's do our best!

383
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:46,620
Sorry!

384
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:52,140
Why here of all places!

385
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,740
Shortcut! Shortcut!

386
00:20:56,860 --> 00:20:57,800
Here it comes!

387
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:00,400
Never mind! Never mind!

388
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:03,920
Light! Light!

389
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:06,400
This guy is worse than he looks!

390
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:08,300
Aaaaaaah!

391
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:36,780
Aaaaaaah!

392
00:21:39,300 --> 00:22:01,300
!

393
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:04,960
Who the hell are you?

394
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,660
Did you see that?

395
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:10,060
I'm the one who arrested the culprit,
you know!

396
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:14,080
What happened?

397
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:21,420
What was I just doing?

398
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:24,780
Did I do it again?

399
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:27,400
So you really don't remember?

400
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:33,520
When I go over the speed limit, my hatred of traffic violations
gets out of control.

401
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:36,000
You're the one who causes the accidents!

402
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:43,100
All of this happens because there
are scum who break the traffic laws.

403
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:47,720
This traffic safety instructor,
seventh dan Tetsuo Ishizu,

404
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:53,120
will make sure the Ishizuru-ryu traffic safety
method is enforced across the whole nation!

405
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:56,280
And to keep myself from going berserk, too.

406
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:03,340
This is amazing.

407
00:23:03,820 --> 00:23:06,220
Ryo-chan,
I hear yesterday was rough for you.

408
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:09,360
Well, the traffic safety
lessons are already brutal.

409
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:10,920
Sorry.

410
00:23:11,340 --> 00:23:12,320
Chief Ishizu.

411
00:23:13,260 --> 00:23:14,300
This guy...

412
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:16,140
What is it, Chief Ishizu?

413
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:18,360
The traffic safety lessons are over, right?

414
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:21,060
Thank you for your hard work yesterday.

415
00:23:21,060 --> 00:23:24,900
So I'm going to have you take the
Ishizuru-ryu traffic safety course

416
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:27,700
and promote you from
seventh rank to sixth rank.

417
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:29,560
Ryo-chan, that's great!

418
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:31,500
Good for you, senpai.

419
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:33,820
No, I'm good, really.

420
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:34,780
What?!

421
00:23:35,230 --> 00:23:36,380
Don't hold back!

422
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:37,340
Understood.

423
00:23:38,380 --> 00:23:41,500
From sixth rank on,
you're allowed to ride a tricycle.

424
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:43,480
Now, follow me.

425
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:44,580
Patrol!

426
00:23:50,140 --> 00:23:52,400
At this rate,
running would honestly be faster.

427
00:23:52,980 --> 00:23:54,800
Hey, wait! Don't go ahead without me!

428
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:58,280
Yeah, I shouldn't have
taken that beginner course.

429
00:24:04,740 --> 00:24:09,040
This is no time to be singing
"Poppo Poppo Heart Poppo"!

430
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:13,720
Why do I have to become a Heart Poppo Tega in
the Special Investigation Division of all things?

431
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:16,180
Chief, please do something about this!

432
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:17,780
Nakagawa, Reiko

433
00:24:17,780 --> 00:24:21,700
Next time,
the birth of Heart Poppo Tega, got it?

434
00:24:35,700 --> 00:24:44,100
Surprise, commotion, spirit,
resolve, swiftness, lending a hand,

435
00:24:44,100 --> 00:24:55,720
decided, inspiration, bouncing,
gathering, action, soaring away.

436
00:24:56,580 --> 00:25:00,580
Above all, incredible power.

437
00:25:00,580 --> 00:25:06,400
Everyone, gather! Come here,

438
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:12,680
the dreamlike, final energy.

439
00:25:13,740 --> 00:25:17,140
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,

440
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:20,020
drawing the universe,
standing on the ground.

441
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:23,840
Kameari's star spun
round and traced a circle.

442
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:27,480
This should be good enough, right?

443
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,940
Like hell it is.

444
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:43,760
Thank you for watching.

